  "report_sha256": "15f28884970be856f78475cdc426604f499998f6f2483ebbaa2760f8e8cc194f",
  "scope": "Six independent matched workers close the case-1120 focus in one 32-entry batch and raise original coverage to 67/83. All methods perform initial full hashes; their worker difference cannot be attributed to reusing cached hashes. A separate replay of the exact append reuses seven unchanged tables but retains the slower complete-sequence result and lack of mean refresh improvement. Initial preparation, guards and full rescans of changed tables are charged. Main persistent schema without temporary name shadowing, ordinary writes and exclusive ownership are preconditions; raw-file tampering and cache mutation are outside the live-cache contract. New cold replay disables fresh discovery and reference search and checks every intermediate catalog, including full seed digests from copied files. It verifies all 4198 reference nodes, preserves all 4153 prior payloads and all 1493 prior artifacts in 29 manifests. Producer and refresh timings ran before tests, paper build, independent replay and preservation checks. Those validations overlapped, so cold elapsed time is not a performance comparison. Measurements share OS caches, use two worker repetitions and three refresh repetitions, and establish no holdout result, confidence interval, peak-RAM reduction, persistent-space reduction, globally minimal expansion or unrestricted-SAT efficiency bound.",
